<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>

<section xml:id="section-hyperbolic-intro" >
<title>Hyperbolic Geometry</title>

<p>Hyperbolic geometry results by replacing the Euclidean parallel postulate with the following.</p>

<axiom><statement><p>Given a line and a point not on that line there exists at least two lines through the point and parallel to the line.</p></statement></axiom>

<exercise>
    <statement>
        <p>There were three major variants of the Euclidean parallel postulate found in <xref ref="list-equivalent-euclidean-postulates" />. Conjecture what each of these looks like in hyperbolic geometry.</p>
    </statement>
</exercise>

</section>
